  "limitations": [
    "The exact direct lifecycle predicate is extracted from production Rust and proved in F*, but this does not prove the surrounding HTTP/BAC/storage composition; the Lean active-pointer and checker-receipt theorems remain independent references.",
    "The models abstract artifact content as two collision-free integer hashes and active versions as v1/v2/v3; they do not model persistence crashes, arbitrary concurrent plan mutation, or multi-artifact dependency graphs.",
    "The persisted checker receipt attests only that a fixed deterministic validator accepted exact bytes and declared claims; it is not a proof of arbitrary artifact semantics, and no Rust-to-Lean refinement is claimed.",
    "The Turso snapshot store, its pre-v7 receipt-less snapshot decoding path, and HTTP transport authentication were removed in PR #2764; no persisted-snapshot migration or transport-authentication claim is retained. Only the in-memory legacy-artifact case (visible for migration, not executable) remains tested."
